    "updated_at": "2017-08-07T20:55:58Z",
    "body": "I don't quite understand why you need to use the 2d context's default path on a recent browser that supports Path2D? The 2D context's default path is a legacy API, and you should not need to use it anymore.\r\n\r\nFor extending an existing path without modifying the original path, this is how you'd do it with Path2D:\r\n\r\n```\r\nvar originalPath = new Path2D();\r\noriginalPath.moveTo(10, 10;);\r\noriginalPath.lineTo(100, 100);\r\n\r\nvar extendedPath = new Path2D();\r\nextendedPath.addPath(originalPath);\r\nextendedPath.lineTo(100, 10);\r\n```\r\n\r\nFYI: addPath() is in the spec, but it is not yet available in all browsers.  It's on the way...\r\n",
